/**
 * TASK: Tell single, double and triple clicks apart.
 *
 * A MouseEvent knows how many clicks in quick succession it is part of:
 * e.getClickCount() is 1 for a single click, 2 for a double click and 3
 * or more for anything faster. Register a MouseListener whose mouseClicked
 * sorts each click into one of three counters and writes the kind of the
 * most recent click into the label named "kind":
 *
 *   click count 1        -> singles() + 1, label "single"
 *   click count 2        -> doubles() + 1, label "double"
 *   click count 3 or more-> rapids()  + 1, label "rapid"
 *
 * Before any click the label reads "none" and all three counters are 0.
 *
 * Example: one single click then one double click ->
 *   singles() is 1, doubles() is 1, label reads "double".
